No Metal on Mavericks: the legacy renderer always draws.

10.9 has no Metal; upstream already falls back to the legacy renderer when
no Metal device exists (metalAllowed: NoGPU). With ITERM_NO_METAL, which
the candidate's targets table sets:

- -[PTYSession metalAllowed:] answers NO with iTermMetalUnavailableReasonNoGPU
  before touching Metal, so the Metal view, driver and glue are never made.
- iTermNoMetal.h declares the few Metal and MetalKit names the legacy path
  still mentions (MTKView as a plain NSView, the MTLDevice protocol); the
  renderer's own headers, Metal.framework and MetalKit.framework are never
  read. iTermMetalDriver.h keeps only its data-source protocol and the
  driver's interface.
- Every reference to a Metal class object is guarded: creating the glue,
  the MTKView and the driver, -metalDevice, -updateMetalDriver, the
  metal context, and the isKindOfClass: tests for MTKView.
- simd comes out of iTermColorMap.h and NSColor+iTerm.h: the vector
  accessors, which only the renderer calls, are behind ITERM_NO_METAL, and
  iTermColorMap.mm's muting arithmetic uses clang's own vector type, since
  the 10.9 SDK has no <simd/>.
- iTermAdvancedGPUSettingsViewController finds no GPUs to choose between.

The renderer's 37 sources are left out by the table's EXCLUDE_SOURCES;
iTermMetalClipView stays, as the scroll view's clip view.

